WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Start with an LLM agent. It proposes a concept and how actions change it. For example: the gripper is no longer empty after picking, and empty after placing.

00:07.000 --> 00:14.000
Learn from what changes. Demonstrated transitions supervise the visual classifier, without hand-labeled concept annotations.

00:14.000 --> 00:23.000
Feedback makes it a loop. The agent reads learning and validation feedback, revises its next proposal, and repeats. The feature animation is schematic.

00:23.000 --> 00:29.000
The result is a concept the robot can recognize: a visual predicate that provides facts for a planner. These outputs illustrate the concept.

00:29.000 --> 00:36.000
Use learned concepts to plan. To store the toys and clean the table, first clear the toys, then grasp the towel, then wipe. Learned preconditions constrain the order.

00:36.000 --> 01:22.500
Complete table-cleaning demonstration: pick and place three toys into the box, grasp the towel, then wipe away the debris. Original footage at three times recorded speed.
